<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix20: Force_SithBladelink ("Sith Warblade") has no Combat Extended support, so CE logs on
       every info-card view:
         Trying to get stat MeleeDamageAverage from Force_SithBladelink which has no support for
         Combat Extended.
         Trying to get stat MeleeArmorPenetration from Force_SithBladelink ...

       WHY IT IS MISSED: a CE patch DOES ship for these mods, but it lives in the *lightsaber* mod
       (3466124712, 1.6/Mods/CE/Patches/ThingDefs_WeaponMelee/Force_Lightsabers.xml, loaded via
       LoadFolders IfModActive=ceteam.combatextended) and only covers Force_LightsaberBase and
       Force_ImbuedBase. Force_SithBladelink is defined in Star Wars : The Force Standalone
       (3557220601, 1.6/Mods/SithSorcery/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/SithArtifact.xml) - the only weapon in
       that mod - and nothing patches it.

       NOT COSMETIC: CE ignores vanilla <armorPenetration> entirely and reads armorPenetrationSharp
       and armorPenetrationBlunt off CombatExtended.ToolCE entries. Without them the weapon does not
       perform as its description claims ("mono-molecular sharpness capable of slicing through even
       the heaviest of armor") against CE armour.

       BENCHMARK: CE's own MeleeWeapon_MonoSwordBladelink, from
       2890901044/Royalty/Patches/Royalty/ThingDefs_Misc/Weapons_RoyaltyBladelinkMelee.xml.
       Chosen over the plain MeleeWeapon_MonoSword because Force_SithBladelink inherits
       BaseWeapon_Bladelink - it is a persona weapon, so the persona monosword is the like-for-like
       reference. Values copied verbatim.

       DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS from the mod author's vanilla numbers, listed so they can be dialled
       back easily:
         - handle power 12 -> 2 with chanceFactor 0.1. CE deliberately makes handle bashes
           incidental; leaving 12 would give a pommel strike comparable to a club.
         - edge power 15 -> 38, point 15 -> 16. CE rebalances melee upward across the board; a
           power-15 edge would leave this well below an ordinary CE monosword despite being a
           late-game artifact.
         - cooldowns 1.6 -> 1.36 / 0.74 / 0.85, matching the persona monosword.
       PRESERVED: the author's capacities (Blunt / Stab / Cut). CE's monosword uses Poke on the
       handle, but changing a capacity changes which ManeuverDef applies, so the author's choice is
       left alone.

       Both mods must be active, so the FindMod wrappers are NESTED - PatchOperationFindMod treats a
       multi-entry <mods> list as OR, not AND.

       success is NOT Always: the FindMod wrappers already make this inert when either mod is
       absent, so an inner failure can only mean the def changed shape, which is what Fix14 taught
       us to hear about rather than have rot silently. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Combat Extended</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
      <mods>
        <li>Star Wars : The Force Standalone</li>
      </mods>
      <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
        <operations>

          <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_SithBladelink"]/tools</xpath>
            <value>
              <tools>
                <li Class="CombatExtended.ToolCE">
                  <label>handle</label>
                  <capacities>
                    <li>Blunt</li>
                  </capacities>
                  <power>2</power>
                  <chanceFactor>0.1</chanceFactor>
                  <cooldownTime>1.36</cooldownTime>
                  <armorPenetrationBlunt>0.605</armorPenetrationBlunt>
                  <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Handle</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
                </li>
                <li Class="CombatExtended.ToolCE">
                  <label>point</label>
                  <capacities>
                    <li>Stab</li>
                  </capacities>
                  <power>16</power>
                  <cooldownTime>0.85</cooldownTime>
                  <armorPenetrationBlunt>1.173</armorPenetrationBlunt>
                  <armorPenetrationSharp>30.24</armorPenetrationSharp>
                </li>
                <li Class="CombatExtended.ToolCE">
                  <label>edge</label>
                  <capacities>
                    <li>Cut</li>
                  </capacities>
                  <power>38</power>
                  <cooldownTime>0.74</cooldownTime>
                  <armorPenetrationBlunt>3.485</armorPenetrationBlunt>
                  <armorPenetrationSharp>21.78</armorPenetrationSharp>
                  <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Edge</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
                </li>
              </tools>
            </value>
          </li>

          <!-- statBases already exists on this def (MarketValue, Mass), so a plain Add is safe. -->
          <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_SithBladelink"]/statBases</xpath>
            <value>
              <Bulk>4</Bulk>
              <MeleeCounterParryBonus>0.50</MeleeCounterParryBonus>
            </value>
          </li>

          <!-- The def has no equippedStatOffsets element, so the element itself is added. -->
          <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_SithBladelink"]</xpath>
            <value>
              <equippedStatOffsets>
                <MeleeCritChance>1.10</MeleeCritChance>
                <MeleeParryChance>0.50</MeleeParryChance>
                <MeleeDodgeChance>0.37</MeleeDodgeChance>
              </equippedStatOffsets>
            </value>
          </li>

        </operations>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
